<section class="page-hero">
  <div class="container page-hero-content">
    <div class="hero-tagline">Legal</div>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="page-hero-sub">What personal data we collect through sensweight.com, why, and what rights you have over it.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container legal">
    <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: 13 October 2026</p>

    <p class="legal-lede">
      This page explains what personal data Unified Cloud Sensors, s.r.o. collects through
      sensweight.com, why, and what rights you have over it. We collect only what you submit
      to us directly through this site&rsquo;s dealer request form &mdash; nothing more.
    </p>

    <div class="legal-section">
      <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
      <p>The data controller for sensweight.com is:</p>
      <p class="legal-address">
        <strong>Unified Cloud Sensors, s.r.o.</strong><br>
        n&aacute;m. V. Mr&scaron;t&iacute;ka 40, 664&nbsp;81 Ostrova&ccaron;ice, Czech Republic<br>
        Company ID (I&Ccaron;): 23272686<br>
        Phone: <a href="tel:+420546427053">+420 546 427 053</a><br>
        Email: <a href="mailto:info@unifiedcloudsensors.com">info@unifiedcloudsensors.com</a>
      </p>
      <p>For any question about this policy or your data, contact us at the email address above.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="legal-section">
      <h2>2. What data we collect</h2>
      <p>
        sensweight.com runs no analytics and sets no cookies of its own. We only collect
        personal data that you choose to type into the one form on this site:
      </p>
      <table class="legal-table">
        <tr><th>Form</th><th>Fields collected</th></tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Dealer / quote request (on <a href="{{ '/how-to-buy/' | localeUrl(lang) }}">How to Buy</a>)</td>
          <td>Name, email address, phone, company, country, area of interest, message</td>
        </tr>
      </table>
      <p>
        We do not request or accept file uploads through this form. If you send us documents
        by email instead, that exchange is handled as ordinary business correspondence, not
        through this website.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="legal-section">
      <h2>3. Why we process it, and our legal basis</h2>
      <p>
        We process what you submit for one purpose: to answer your request and, where relevant,
        to prepare a quote or put you in touch with a dealer.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Processed under GDPR Art. 6(1)(b) &mdash; steps taken at your request prior to a
          possible contract &mdash; or, where no contract is in prospect, Art. 6(1)(f), our
          legitimate interest in responding to inbound business inquiries.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We do not use your data for marketing, profiling, or automated decision-making, and we
        do not sell or rent it to any third party.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="legal-section">
      <h2>4. How your submission is handled</h2>
      <p>
        When you submit the form, your data is sent to a backend service we operate (AWS Lambda
        and Amazon API Gateway, in the <strong>eu-central-1 (Frankfurt)</strong> AWS region)
        which:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>sends one notification email containing your submission to our sales inbox, and</li>
        <li>sends one automatic confirmation email back to the address you provided,</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        both via Amazon Simple Email Service (SES). <strong>Your submission is not written to
        any database.</strong> The backend keeps no persistent copy &mdash; once the two emails
        are sent, the only copies that exist are the emails themselves, in our company mailbox
        and in the mailbox you submitted.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="legal-section">
      <h2>5. Bot protection on the form</h2>
      <p>
        The form is protected by <strong>Cloudflare Turnstile</strong>, which checks whether a
        submission comes from a person or an automated script. To make that check, the widget
        loads from Cloudflare and sends your IP address together with technical signals about
        your browser and device to Cloudflare, and may store a short-lived token in your browser
        for the check itself. Cloudflare does not receive the contents of the form, and the
        check runs only on the page that carries the form.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="legal-section">
      <h2>6. Who we share data with</h2>
      <p>
        We do not sell your data. It passes through the following processors, strictly to
        operate the site and deliver the emails above:
      </p>
      <table class="legal-table">
        <tr><th>Processor</th><th>Role</th><th>Location</th></tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Amazon Web Services (AWS)</td>
          <td>Site hosting (S3 and the CloudFront CDN), form backend, and email delivery (SES)</td>
          <td>Stored in the EU (Frankfurt, eu-central-1); pages are served from CDN edge
            locations worldwide, so a request may be answered from outside the EU</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Cloudflare</td>
          <td>Turnstile bot check on the dealer request form (see section 5)</td>
          <td>Global infrastructure</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Google (Google Fonts)</td>
          <td>Loads this site&rsquo;s typefaces (Chakra Petch, IBM Plex Sans/Mono) directly from
            Google&rsquo;s servers</td>
          <td>Google infrastructure (may be outside the EU)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>jsDelivr</td>
          <td>Loads the charting library used by the live demo dashboards</td>
          <td>Global CDN; only on the demo pages, not on the rest of the site</td>
        </tr>
      </table>
      <p>
        Loading a font or a script this way sends your browser&rsquo;s IP address to that
        provider as a normal part of the request &mdash; this happens on page load, not only
        when you submit a form, and applies to all visitors. Neither Google nor jsDelivr
        receives any of the form data.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="legal-section">
      <h2>7. How long we keep it</h2>
      <div class="legal-note">
        <strong>Draft placeholder &mdash; confirm before relying on this.</strong> We have not
        yet adopted a formal retention schedule for this mailbox. Until one exists, submitted
        emails should be treated as retained only for as long as reasonably needed to answer the
        inquiry and complete any resulting business relationship, and deleted afterwards. A firm
        number here (for example &ldquo;12 months&rdquo; or &ldquo;3 years&rdquo;) is a business
        and legal decision, not something to take from the code.
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="legal-section">
      <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
      <p>Under the GDPR, you have the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>request access to the personal data we hold about you;</li>
        <li>request correction of inaccurate data;</li>
        <li>request erasure of your data;</li>
        <li>object to or request restriction of our processing;</li>
        <li>request a copy of your data in a portable format; and</li>
        <li>withdraw consent at any time, where processing is based on consent.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        To exercise any of these rights, email
        <a href="mailto:info@unifiedcloudsensors.com">info@unifiedcloudsensors.com</a>. You also
        have the right to lodge a complaint with the Czech data protection authority:
      </p>
      <p class="legal-address">
        &Uacute;&rcaron;ad pro ochranu osobn&iacute;ch &uacute;daj&uring; (Office for Personal Data Protection)<br>
        Pplk. Sochora 27, 170&nbsp;00 Praha 7, Czech Republic<br>
        <a href="https://www.uoou.cz" target="_blank" rel="noopener">www.uoou.cz</a>
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="legal-section">
      <h2>9. Cookies and tracking</h2>
      <p>
        This site sets no cookies of its own and runs no analytics, advertising, or tracking
        scripts. The only browser storage involved is the short-lived token the Turnstile bot
        check may use, described in section 5. If this changes in the future &mdash; for example
        if we add analytics &mdash; this policy will be updated first and, where the law requires
        it, a cookie consent notice will be added before any non-essential cookie is set.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="legal-section">
      <h2>10. Children</h2>
      <p>
        This site is intended for business use and is not directed at children. We do not
        knowingly collect personal data from anyone under 16.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="legal-section">
      <h2>11. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy as the site or our data practices change. The
        &ldquo;Last updated&rdquo; date at the top of this page reflects the most recent
        revision.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
